"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nThe setting of announcing a murder through a newspaper advertisement is original.  \n> “A murder is announced. Friday, October 29th, at 6:30 PM. Place: Little Paddocks. Those who are interested are welcome.”\n\nThe residents think this advertisement is either a play or a joke, and some come to the Little Paddocks mansion out of curiosity.  \nThe owner of the mansion is flustered but welcomes the guests, and when the set time arrives, a sudden power outage occurs.  \n\nAt that moment, a gunshot rings out, and an intruder enters but is shot dead on the spot.  \n\nThe play seemed to end as an attempted murder by the intruder, but a new truth is revealed by .  \n\nThe family tree was complicated, so it was a bit difficult, but I read it with interest because the setting was unique.  \n"